  ⊘ gain_core (native/src/gain) — missing from stale_lib_static
  These build, and their symbols ship in neither lib<pkg>.so nor lib<pkg>.a,
  so the installed header declares functions a C consumer cannot link. Python
  is unaffected — the extension links each core directly — which is why this
  goes unnoticed. `jm apply` writes the missing target_sources() line. Keep a
  core out of the library on purpose by naming `CMakeLists.txt:<core>` in
  [project] status_allow; naming `CMakeLists.txt` itself exempts every core,
  for a project that links its cores its own way.

