  A unit that exists ONLY on disk refuses the flip: the render
  does not produce it, so flipping would delete it. Move it to
  the `_extra.c` beside the fragment, which is already wired.
  A member whose BINDING accepts more than the manifest
  declares refuses too: there the file is ahead, so flipping
  removes a feature. Declare it in the manifest first.
  A unit that DIFFERS needs your eyes: jm cannot tell a
  hand-written body from a render that predates a codegen
  change, which is why it asks rather than guesses.
  `adds only`: the render keeps every token of the unit and
  adds code (a guard, keywords) -- nothing on disk is lost.
  `jm adopt <obj> --accept-additions` takes those; a `differs`
  unit removes code, and is taken only by name:
  `--accept <unit>`.

